### IPP-401 Languages API tests
### How to use: run `npm run dev` in /server, then click "Send Request" above each request, top to bottom.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api

### Admin login: put the ADMIN_EMAIL / ADMIN_PASSWORD from server/.env here.
### Do NOT commit this file with the real password (put it back to CHANGE_ME after testing).
@adminEmail = raeeschechi302@gmail.com
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME

### Tokens are picked up automatically from the login requests below
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.token}}
@langId = {{newLang.response.body.data.language._id}}


### 1. Public list (no login) -> expect 200, PHP with qaCount 20, mcqCount 20, freeQaCount 5
GET {{baseUrl}}/languages


### 2. One language by slug -> expect 200 with PHP details and counts
GET {{baseUrl}}/languages/php


### 3. Unknown slug -> expect 404 "Language not found"
GET {{baseUrl}}/languages/cobol


### 4. Add a language WITHOUT login -> expect 401 "Please log in to continue"
POST {{baseUrl}}/languages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test Language"
}


### 5. Admin login -> expect 200 (the token is saved for the requests below)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}


### 6. Add with bad data -> expect 400 "Name is required"
POST {{baseUrl}}/languages
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "slug": "Bad Slug!"
}


### 7. Add a language -> expect 201 "Language added", slug "c-plus-plus" made from the name
# @name newLang
POST {{baseUrl}}/languages
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "C++",
  "icon": "cplusplus",
  "description": "Test language for IPP-401"
}


### 8. Add the same name again -> expect 409 "... already exists"
POST {{baseUrl}}/languages
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "C++"
}


### 9. Deactivate it -> expect 200 "Language updated", isActive false
PUT {{baseUrl}}/languages/{{langId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isActive": false
}


### 10. Public list -> expect only PHP (C++ is hidden because it is inactive)
GET {{baseUrl}}/languages


### 11. Admin list with ?all=true -> expect C++ AND PHP
GET {{baseUrl}}/languages?all=true
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 12. Try to delete PHP (it has 40 questions) -> expect 409 "PHP has 40 questions. Deactivate it instead..."
###     First copy PHP's "_id" from request 1 and paste it below in place of PHP_ID_HERE.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/languages/6ad894999dcf1f882fd249b2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 13. Delete the test language (no questions) -> expect 200 "Language deleted"
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/languages/{{langId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 14. Bad id -> expect 400 "Invalid language id"
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/languages/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
